---
// Resurface marketing landing page. Ported verbatim from the original standalone HTML
// into an Astro page: styles are `is:global` and scripts are `is:inline` so the output
// is byte-for-byte equivalent to the hand-tuned original (content + SEO preserved).
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />

    <!-- ===== SEO ===== -->
    <title>Resurface — Retro Action Item Tracker for Jira | OutpostLabs</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Resurface turns retro & sprint action items into owned, due-dated Jira issues that resurface until they're done. Auto-nudges owners, tracks carry-overs, proves follow-through. Free for up to 10 users. Runs on Atlassian." />
    <meta name="keywords" content="Jira retro action items, retrospective action item tracker, sprint action items Jira, retro follow-up, action item accountability, agile retrospective Jira, scrum action items" />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://outpostlabs.dev/resurface/" />
    <meta name="robots" content="index, follow" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#0E1726" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />

    <!-- Open Graph / Twitter -->
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Resurface by OutpostLabs" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Resurface — Retro Action Item Tracker for Jira" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Owned, due-dated retro & sprint action items that resurface in Jira until they're done. Free for up to 10 users. Runs on Atlassian." />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://outpostlabs.dev/resurface/" />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://outpostlabs.dev/resurface/resurface-hero-960x600.png" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="Resurface — Retro Action Item Tracker for Jira" />
    <meta name="twitter:description" content="Retro action items that don't die: owned, due-dated, and resurfaced in Jira until they're done." />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content="https://outpostlabs.dev/resurface/resurface-hero-960x600.png" />

    <!-- Structured data -->
    <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>
      {
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@type": "SoftwareApplication",
        "name": "Resurface — Retro Action Item Tracker & Accountability",
        "applicationCategory": "BusinessApplication",
        "operatingSystem": "Atlassian Jira Cloud",
        "description": "Turn retro and sprint action items into owned, due-dated Jira issues that resurface until they're done. Auto-nudges owners, tracks carry-overs, and reports follow-through with accountability metrics.",
        "url": "https://outpostlabs.dev/resurface/",
        "downloadUrl": "https://marketplace.atlassian.com/apps/3449871240/resurface-retro-action-item-tracker-accountability",
        "offers": { "@type": "Offer", "price": "0", "priceCurrency": "USD", "description": "Free for up to 10 users" },
        "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "OutpostLabs", "url": "https://outpostlabs.dev" }
      }
    </script>
    <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>
      {
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "mainEntity": [
          {"@type":"Question","name":"Does Resurface work with my existing retro tool?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Resurface is tool-agnostic. It works alongside any retrospective app because it tracks action items as native Jira issues, so there's nothing to switch."}},
          {"@type":"Question","name":"Where does my data go?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Nowhere. Resurface is built on Atlassian Forge and carries the Runs on Atlassian badge, so your data never leaves Atlassian Cloud."}},
          {"@type":"Question","name":"Is Resurface free?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Resurface is free for up to 10 users, billed through the Atlassian Marketplace after that."}},
          {"@type":"Question","name":"How is it different from a retro board?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A retro board helps you run the meeting. Resurface handles what happens after: it makes sure the action items get an owner and a due date, resurface when overdue, and actually get done."}}
        ]
      }
    </script>

    <style is:global>
      :root{
        --navy:#0E1726; --navy2:#132038; --ink:#101B2E; --slate:#5A6B85;
        --paper:#F7F9FC; --line:#E7ECF3;
        --amber1:#FFC24B; --amber2:#FF7A2F; --amber:#FF7A2F;
        --white:#FFFFFF; --muted:#A9B8CE; --red:#E5484D; --green:#22C55E;
        --maxw:1080px;
      }
      *{box-sizing:border-box}
      html{scroll-behavior:smooth}
      body{margin:0;font-family:'Inter',-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:var(--ink);background:var(--white);line-height:1.55;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased}
      a{color:inherit}
      .wrap{max-width:var(--maxw);margin:0 auto;padding:0 24px}
      .btn{display:inline-block;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 22px;transition:transform .06s ease, box-shadow .2s ease}
      .btn:active{transform:translateY(1px)}
      .btn-primary{background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--amber1),var(--amber2));color:#2a1400;box-shadow:0 8px 22px rgba(255,122,47,.28)}
      .btn-ghost{border:1.5px solid rgba(255,255,255,.28);color:#fff}
      .btn-dark{background:var(--ink);color:#fff}
      .chips{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px}
      .chip{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:#D7E1EF;background:#16233A;border:1px solid #2A3A57;border-radius:20px;padding:7px 14px}
      .chip .dot{width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--amber1),var(--amber2))}
      .eyebrow{font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:1.6px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--amber)}

      /* header */
      header{background:var(--navy);position:sticky;top:0;z-index:20;border-bottom:1px solid #1c2942}
      .nav{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;height:66px}
      .brand{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-weight:800;font-size:19px}
      .brand .logo{width:38px;height:38px;flex:none}
      .brand small{display:block;font-weight:500;font-size:11px;color:#8DA0BC;letter-spacing:.2px;margin-top:-2px}
      .nav .btn{padding:10px 18px;font-size:14px}
      .nav-right{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:20px}
      .nav-right .navlink{color:#c8d5e6;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px}
      .nav-right .navlink:hover{color:#fff}
      @media(max-width:560px){.nav-right .navlink{display:none}}

      /* hero */
      .hero{background:radial-gradient(1100px 500px at 80% -10%, #1b2c4b 0%, var(--navy) 55%);color:#fff;padding:74px 0 84px}
      .hero-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.05fr .95fr;gap:48px;align-items:center}
      h1{font-size:52px;line-height:1.06;letter-spacing:-1.5px;margin:14px 0 18px;font-weight:800}
      h1 .amber{background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--amber1),var(--amber2));-webkit-background-clip:text;background-clip:text;color:transparent}
      .lede{font-size:19px;color:var(--muted);max-width:520px;margin:0 0 28px}
      .cta-row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:14px;margin-bottom:26px}

      /* product card mock */
      .card{background:#fff;border-radius:18px;box-shadow:0 24px 60px rgba(0,0,0,.38);padding:22px 22px 20px;color:var(--ink)}
      .card .top{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center}
      .pill-red{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;background:#FDE7E7;color:#C42B2F;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;border-radius:13px;padding:5px 11px}
      .pill-red .d{width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--red)}
      .card h3{font-size:21px;margin:12px 0 14px;color:var(--ink)}
      .owner{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:11px}
      .avatar{width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:50%;background:#3D5A99;color:#fff;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center}
      .owner .due{color:var(--red);font-weight:600;font-size:13px}
      .owner .name{font-weight:600;font-size:14.5px;color:#26344B}
      .divider{height:1px;background:var(--line);margin:16px 0}
      .card .foot{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center}
      .card .carry{color:var(--slate);font-weight:600;font-size:14px}
      .tag-amber{background:#FFF3E6;color:#C25A12;font-weight:700;font-size:12.5px;border-radius:14px;padding:5px 12px}
      .nudge{margin-top:16px;background:var(--ink);color:#E8EEF5;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:600;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 14px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px}
      .clock{width:15px;height:15px;flex:none}

      /* sections */
      section{padding:76px 0}
      .section-head{text-align:center;max-width:680px;margin:0 auto 46px}
      .section-head h2{font-size:34px;letter-spacing:-.8px;margin:10px 0 12px}
      .section-head p{color:var(--slate);font-size:18px;margin:0}
      .alt{background:var(--paper)}

      .steps{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:24px}
      .step{background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:16px;padding:26px}
      .alt .step{background:#fff}
      .step .ic{width:46px;height:46px;border-radius:12px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fff2e0,#ffe3cc);margin-bottom:16px}
      .step h3{font-size:19px;margin:0 0 8px}
      .step p{color:var(--slate);margin:0;font-size:15.5px}

      .why{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px 40px;max-width:900px;margin:0 auto}
      .why .row{display:flex;gap:13px;align-items:flex-start}
      .check{color:var(--green);flex:none;margin-top:2px}
      .why h4{margin:0 0 3px;font-size:16.5px}
      .why p{margin:0;color:var(--slate);font-size:15px}

      /* cta band */
      .band{background:var(--navy);color:#fff;text-align:center;border-radius:24px;padding:56px 28px;margin:0 24px}
      .band h2{font-size:32px;letter-spacing:-.6px;margin:0 0 10px}
      .band p{color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 26px;font-size:17px}

      /* email / kit */
      .email-box{max-width:560px;margin:0 auto;text-align:center}
      .email-box h2{font-size:28px;margin:0 0 8px;letter-spacing:-.5px}
      .email-box p{color:var(--slate);margin:0 0 22px}
      .kitform{display:flex;gap:10px;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap}
      .kitform input[type=email]{flex:1;min-width:240px;max-width:340px;padding:14px 16px;border:1.5px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;font-size:15px;font-family:inherit}
      .kitform input[type=email]:focus{outline:none;border-color:var(--amber)}
      .fineprint{color:#8a99ad;font-size:12.5px;margin-top:12px}

      /* faq */
      .faq{max-width:760px;margin:0 auto}
      details{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:4px 20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:#fff}
      summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:700;padding:16px 0;list-style:none;font-size:16.5px}
      summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}
      details[open] summary{color:var(--amber)}
      details p{color:var(--slate);margin:0 0 16px;font-size:15.5px}

      /* footer */
      footer{background:var(--navy);color:#9fb0c8;padding:44px 0;font-size:14px}
      .foot{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:16px}
      .foot a{color:#c8d5e6;text-decoration:none;margin-left:20px}
      .foot a:hover{color:#fff}

      @media(max-width:860px){
        .hero-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:36px}
        h1{font-size:40px}
        .steps{grid-template-columns:1fr}
        .why{grid-template-columns:1fr}
        .section-head h2{font-size:28px}
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header>
      <div class="wrap nav">
        <a class="brand" href="/resurface/" aria-label="Resurface home">
          <!-- beacon mark -->
          <svg class="logo" viewBox="0 0 32 32" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true">
            <rect width="32" height="32" rx="8" fill="rgba(255,255,255,0.16)" stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.4)" />
            <g stroke="#fff" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <g stroke-width="2.3">
                <path d="M6 20 L11.5 20" />
                <path d="M20.5 20 L26 20" />
                <path d="M11.5 20 L9.8 17.8" />
                <path d="M20.5 20 L22.2 17.8" />
              </g>
              <g stroke-width="2.7">
                <path d="M16 25 L16 9.5" />
                <path d="M11.6 14 L16 9.5 L20.4 14" />
              </g>
            </g>
          </svg>
          <span>Resurface<small>by OutpostLabs.dev</small></span>
        </a>
        <div class="nav-right">
          <a class="navlink" href="/">Home</a>
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://marketplace.atlassian.com/apps/3449871240/resurface-retro-action-item-tracker-accountability">Install free</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- HERO -->
    <div class="hero">
      <div class="wrap hero-grid">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow">Retro action item tracker for Jira</div>
          <h1>Action items<br /><span class="amber">that don't die.</span></h1>
          <p class="lede">Retros are easy. Follow-through isn't. Resurface turns retro & sprint action items into owned, due-dated Jira issues that resurface until they're actually done.</p>
          <div class="cta-row">
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://marketplace.atlassian.com/apps/3449871240/resurface-retro-action-item-tracker-accountability">Install free on the Atlassian Marketplace</a>
            <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="#how">See how it works</a>
          </div>
          <div class="chips">
            <span class="chip"><span class="dot"></span>Runs on Atlassian</span>
            <span class="chip">Free for up to 10 users</span>
            <span class="chip">Works with any retro tool</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- product mock (mirrors the app) -->
        <div class="card" role="img" aria-label="A Jira action item that is overdue, assigned to Maria P., carried over twice, and automatically resurfaced with a nudge to the owner.">
          <div class="top">
            <span class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--amber)">Action item</span>
            <span class="pill-red"><span class="d"></span>Overdue</span>
          </div>
          <h3>Fix flaky checkout test</h3>
          <div class="owner">
            <span class="avatar">MP</span>
            <span>
              <span class="name">Maria P.</span><br />
              <span class="due">Due Jun 24 · 3 days late</span>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="divider"></div>
          <div class="foot">
            <span class="carry">&#8635; Carried over &#215;2</span>
            <span class="tag-amber">&#8593; Resurfaced</span>
          </div>
          <div class="nudge">
            <svg class="clock" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#FFB020" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="13" r="8"></circle><path d="M12 13V8M12 13l3 2" stroke-linecap="round"></path></svg>
            Overdue — owner nudged in Jira
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- PROBLEM -->
    <section>
      <div class="wrap section-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">The problem</div>
        <h2>Great retro. Then the action items vanish.</h2>
        <p>Every retro ends with a tidy list of things to fix. Two weeks later, half of them are gone — no owner, no due date, nobody chasing them — and you're writing the same ones down again. Resurface makes sure that doesn't happen.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- HOW / FEATURES -->
    <section id="how" class="alt">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div class="eyebrow">How it works</div>
          <h2>Capture. Resurface. Prove.</h2>
          <p>One job, done well — right where the work already lives, in Jira.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="steps">
          <div class="step">
            <div class="ic">🎯</div>
            <h3>Every item gets an owner & a deadline</h3>
            <p>Mark any Jira issue as a tracked action item with an enforced owner and due date, tagged by source: retro, sprint, or manual.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="step">
            <div class="ic">🔔</div>
            <h3>Overdue items resurface — automatically</h3>
            <p>A scheduled nudge comments on the issue and notifies the owner, and a carry-over count shows how often a task has slipped.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="step">
            <div class="ic">📊</div>
            <h3>Prove follow-through</h3>
            <p>Closure rate, average age, overdue count, % carried over, and repeat slippage by owner — the accountability view for team leads.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- WHY -->
    <section>
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div class="eyebrow">Why teams pick it</div>
          <h2>Small, focused, and out of your way</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="why">
          <div class="row"><svg class="check" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg><div><h4>Works with any retro tool</h4><p>It's not another retro board. Keep the tool you love — Resurface just handles the follow-through in Jira.</p></div></div>
          <div class="row"><svg class="check" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg><div><h4>Runs on Atlassian</h4><p>Built on Forge, so your data never leaves Atlassian Cloud. No external servers, no data trips.</p></div></div>
          <div class="row"><svg class="check" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg><div><h4>Free for up to 10 users</h4><p>Try it on a real team at no cost. Billing is handled cleanly through the Atlassian Marketplace.</p></div></div>
          <div class="row"><svg class="check" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg><div><h4>Set up in minutes</h4><p>Install, mark an issue as an action item, done. Nothing to configure, no training required.</p></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA BAND -->
    <section style="padding:40px 0">
      <div class="band">
        <h2>Stop losing action items.</h2>
        <p>Install Resurface and give your next retro some teeth.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://marketplace.atlassian.com/apps/3449871240/resurface-retro-action-item-tracker-accountability">Install free on the Atlassian Marketplace</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- EMAIL / KIT -->
    <section class="alt" id="updates">
      <div class="wrap email-box">
        <div class="eyebrow">Stay in the loop</div>
        <h2>New apps & Jira tips from OutpostLabs</h2>
        <p>We're building a family of small, focused tools. Drop your email for occasional updates — no spam, unsubscribe anytime.</p>

        <!-- Kit (ConvertKit) form. Replace REPLACE_FORM_ID with your Kit form ID.
             Prefer inline behavior? Delete this <form> and paste your Kit JavaScript embed snippet instead. -->
        <form class="kitform" action="https://app.kit.com/forms/9637468/subscriptions" method="post" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <input type="email" name="email_address" placeholder="you@company.com" aria-label="Email address" required />
          <button class="btn btn-dark" type="submit">Keep me posted</button>
        </form>
        <p class="fineprint">Powered by Kit. We'll only email you about product updates.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- FAQ -->
    <section>
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div class="eyebrow">FAQ</div>
          <h2>Questions, answered</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="faq">
          <details open><summary>Does Resurface work with my existing retro tool?</summary><p>Yes. Resurface is tool-agnostic — it works alongside any retrospective app because it tracks action items as native Jira issues. There's nothing to switch.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Where does my data go?</summary><p>Nowhere. Resurface is built on Atlassian Forge and carries the "Runs on Atlassian" badge, so your data never leaves Atlassian Cloud.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Is it really free?</summary><p>It's free for up to 10 users. Above that, it's billed per user through the Atlassian Marketplace — no separate account or card needed.</p></details>
          <details><summary>How is this different from a retro board?</summary><p>A retro board helps you run the meeting. Resurface handles what happens after: it makes sure action items get an owner and a due date, resurface when overdue, and actually get closed.</p></details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer>
      <div class="wrap foot">
        <div>© <span id="yr"></span> OutpostLabs.dev — small, focused apps that do one thing well.</div>
        <div>
          <a href="/">OutpostLabs</a>
          <a href="https://marketplace.atlassian.com/apps/3449871240/resurface-retro-action-item-tracker-accountability">Marketplace</a>
          <a href="/resurface/docs/">Docs</a>
          <a href="/resurface/privacy/">Privacy</a>
          <a href="/resurface/terms/">Terms</a>
          <a href="/resurface/sla/">SLA</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </footer>

    <script is:inline>
      document.getElementById('yr').textContent = new Date().getFullYear();
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
